<br>
I believe you are misinterpreting the text, but agree that it could be<br>
made more clear.<br>
<br>
Suppose that the ClientHello includes a supported_versions extensions<br>
that contains two values, TLS 1.4 and TLS 1.0, and the server supports<br>
TLS 1.3 and below. My interpretation of the current draft is that the<br>
server MUST use the supported_versions extension to determine the<br>
client&#39;s preference, but then once deciding to use TLS 1.0 for the<br>
connection sends a normal TLS 1.0 ServerHello, with version field set to<br=
>
0x0300 and no supported_versions extension. Note that Section 4.2.1 says<br=
>
that<br>
<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 A server which negotiates TLS 1.3 MUST respo=
nd by sending a<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 &quot;supported_versions&quot; extension con=
taining the selected version<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 value (0x0304).<br>
<br>
It says nothing about a server that negotiates an earlier version.<br>
<br>
If my understanding is correct, then I believe the text in Section 4.1.3<br=
>
could be made more clear. Draft -21 said that the version field of<br>
ServerHello &quot;contains the version of TLS negotiated for this<br>
connection.&quot; (this is similar to what RFC 5246 said). The current draf=
t<br>
says:<br>
<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 In TLS 1.3, the TLS server indicates i=
ts version using the<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 &quot;supported_versions&quot; extensi=
on (Section 4.2.1), and the<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 legacy_version field MUST be set to 0x=
0303, which is the<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 version number for TLS 1.2.<br>
<br>
To be consistent with RFC 5246 and earlier, it seems like the text<br>
should say something like:<br>
<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 For a TLS 1.3 ServerHello the TLS serv=
er indicates its version<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 using the &quot;supported_versions&quo=
t; extension (Section 4.2.1), and<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 the legacy_version field MUST be set t=
o 0x0303, which is the<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 version number for TLS 1.2. For a TLS =
1.2 and earlier ServerHello<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 the legacy_version field contains the =
version of TLS negotiated<br>
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 for this connection.<br>
<br>
On Thu, Mar 1, 2018 at 5:24 AM, Nikos Mavrogiannopoulos<br>
&lt;<a href=3D"mailto:nmav@redhat.com" target=3D"_blank">nmav@redhat.com</a=
